    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] Henriette Catherine de Joyeuse (8 January 1585 – 25 February 1656) was the daughter of Henri de Joyeuse and Catherine de Nogaret.\n[2] Blanche of Navarre (1226 – 12 August 1283), also known as Blanche of Champagne, was the daughter of Theobald the Troubador, King of Navarre and Count of Champagne, and his second wife Agnes of Beaujeu.\n[3] Marie Louise Gonzaga (Polish: \"Ludwika Maria\" ; 18 August 1611 – 10 May 1667) was a French princess, noblewoman, the wife of two Polish kings and Grand Dukes of Lithuania, Władysław IV Vasa and John II Casimir, and as such queen of Poland and Grand Duchess of Lithuania.\n[4] Joan married Philip of Évreux, who was also a member of the French royal family.\n\nNotes:\n[bridge] Catherine of Guise was the mother of Marie Louise Gonzaga."
